B.u119. {"problem": "The change widens who may approve commits, which is a permission element. The authoring domain's own rule says such an element needs a second person's confirmation, but nothing here marks it as a permission element or asks for that confirmation. In the file as it stands, approve_commit shows status: confirmed with a new interview ref (L49) and no quote, so it reads as confirmed without that process.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.approve_commit (source/status) and actions.confirm_element / second-person precondition", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
