B.u127. {"problem": "The diff sets `approve_commit` and its `checks-pass` and `not-approved` preconditions to `status: proposed`. The files after the change still show them as `confirmed`, so the diff and the resulting file disagree. The two preconditions were confirmed by an unrelated earlier interview line (L6), and this change does not touch them, so downgrading them regresses confirmed rules. Separately, this is an element about who may approve. Under `confirm_element`, `second-person` and `second_confirm_element`, it needs a second person's confirmation, and the new source ref (L49) carries no quote to show that happened.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.approve_commit status and preconditions; second-person rule", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
