B.u121. {"problem": "The description says the owner names a deputy who approves while the owner is away, but nothing in the domain does this. No action names or revokes a deputy, no field or object holds the deputy, and no precondition checks that the owner is away. Any deputy can approve at any time, so the owner-only approval rule is effectively dropped.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, roles.deputy and actions.approve_commit (actor, description)", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
B.u116. {"problem": "The change is inconsistent about the approval rule's confirmation state. The diff sets approve_commit and its two preconditions (checks-pass, not-approved) to status: proposed, but the post-change file shows them as confirmed. The preconditions were not part of this request, yet the diff downgrades them. They still cite the old interview line L6, and the action now cites the new L49 with no quote. The deputy rule is therefore either unconfirmed in the deployed domain or wrongly marked confirmed. As an element about who may approve, it also needs the two-person confirmation that confirm_element requires.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: actions.approve_commit status, source and preconditions checks-pass and not-approved", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
